@startuml FR01_Organizations_Sequence
title FR-01 - Maintain and View Organizations
autonumber
actor "Administrator / Authorized Staff" as Actor
boundary "Client" as Client
control "OrganizationController" as Ctrl
control "OrganizationService" as Svc
database "Database" as DB
Actor -> Client: Select operation; enter relevant data or changes
Client -> Ctrl: Submit operation and organization/data
Ctrl -> Ctrl: Check authentication, permission and scope
alt Access denied
  Ctrl --> Client: Deny access
  Client --> Actor: Display access denial
else Access permitted
  alt UC-01.5 - View Organizations
    Ctrl -> Svc: Request permitted organizations or details
    Svc -> DB: Retrieve permitted organizations or details
    DB --> Svc: Organization data
    Svc --> Ctrl: Permitted organization data
    Ctrl --> Client: Return organization data
    Client --> Actor: Display organizations or details
  else UC-01.4 - Deactivate Organization (Administrator)
    Ctrl -> Svc: Deactivate selected organization
    Svc -> DB: Set active = false; preserve referenced records
    DB --> Svc: Updated organization
    Svc --> Ctrl: Organization details
    Ctrl --> Client: Return organization details
    Client --> Actor: Display inactive organization
  else UC-01.1 / UC-01.2 / UC-01.3 - Create or Edit (Administrator)
    Ctrl -> Svc: Validate bank/hospital data or changes
    Svc -> Svc: Validate details and required coordinates
    Svc -> DB: Check for duplicate data
    DB --> Svc: Duplicate-check result
    alt Invalid or duplicate data
      Svc --> Ctrl: Validation or duplicate error
      Ctrl --> Client: Return error
      Client --> Actor: Return to form for correction
    else Valid data
      Svc -> DB: Save bank/hospital record or changes
      DB --> Svc: Organization identifier and details
      Svc --> Ctrl: Saved organization
      Ctrl --> Client: Return identifier and details
      Client --> Actor: Display organization details
    end
  end
end
note over Svc, DB
  Active banks and requesting hospitals require
  validated latitude and longitude.
  Editing and deactivation preserve linked history.
end note
@enduml